</mjx-container></span> is congruent to\na diagonal matrix all of whose entries are <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\pm1\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cB1\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</li>\n<li>Give two real symmetric <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"2 \\times\n2\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cD7\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> matrices that are congruent and have no eigenvalue in\ncommon.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n<p><em>Hint for (b): recall from <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exm-congruence-first\">@exm-congruence-first</span> (b) what\nscaling a basis vector does to a diagonal entry.</em></p>","file":"ch14-forms/02-congruence.html"}